{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Webhooks Documentation",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "# Webhooks content\n\nThe webhook content includes the type of the webhook, a signature calculated from the API key, and data that depends on the type of webhook.\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"event\": \"membership.created\",\n  \"signature\": \"...\",\n  \"data\": {\n    id: 1,\n    \"firstName\": \"John\",\n    \"lastName\": \"Doe\",\n    \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n    ...\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Signature Creation\n\nThe signature for the webhook is created using HMAC SHA-256.\nHere is an example to verify the signature with javascript:\n\n```js\nconst body = await request.json();\nconst date = body.date;\n\nif (new Date().getTime() - date <= 60 * 1 * 1000) {\n  console.log(\"Valid date\");\n\n  const keyBuffer = new TextEncoder().encode(apiKey);\n  const cryptoKey = await crypto.subtle.importKey(\"raw\", keyBuffer, { name: \"HMAC\", hash: { name: \"SHA-256\" } }, false, [\"verify\"]);\n  const { signature, ...data } = body;\n  const dataBuffer = new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(data));\n  const match = signature.match(/.{1,2}/g);\n  if (!match) return;\n  const signatureArray = new Uint8Array(match.map((byte: string) => parseInt(byte, 16)));\n  const valid = await crypto.subtle.verify(\"HMAC\", cryptoKey, signatureArray, dataBuffer);\n  if (valid) {\n    console.log(\"Valid signature\");\n    // handle webhook\n  } else {\n    console.log(\"Invalid signature\");\n  }\n} else {\n  console.log(\"Invalid date\");\n  // avoid replay attack\n}\n```\n\n## SmartLink SDK\n\nUse our [Javascript SDK](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@vaultys/smartlink-sdk) to verify your webhooks and use the SmartLink API.\n\n```bash\nnpm i @vaultys/smartlink-sdk\n```\n"
  },
